# rt39 TDD reds and controls, Runtime flow
#
# WHAT THIS IS: a live re-run transcript, not a summary. The reds and controls were first run during
# implementation but their output was never captured to a file, so every line below was produced by
# re-running the same scripts at the tree and stamp in each section header. Script md5s are recorded so a
# reader can re-run them.
#
# WHAT EACH SECTION PROVES
#   item five RED  the retention shape gen_round.py writes today is NOT reproducible: two collects of one
#                  source differ, because the member stores the output file name and the wall-clock mtime.
#                  The changed shape gives mtime 0, no stored name, and one digest.
#   controls       item five's POSITIVE control reproduces the two COMMITTED archives byte for byte, which
#                  is what rules out "reproducible but different from what is already committed";
#                  item one reproduces all three committed group figures from the committed artifact and
#                  carries its own red; item four proves the sources digest is carried and compared, and
#                  measures the pre-change defect on the committed index.
#
# SCRATCH ROOT: every control writes under the flow's own self-test root, never the shared /tmp (F-001).
# An earlier version of control_item4 used the shared /tmp; moving it exposed that its own cleanup guard
# had the same assumption and refused to remove a directory outside /tmp, so the guard was pointed at the
# root the script actually writes to. Both are fixed here and the removal line below shows the new root.
#

